Ok, I just took a quick look at the Adept paper.  Basically, we're talking about doing the expression template pattern that Eigen uses to do autodiff and extending it to higher order derivatives?  That makes sense to me, but I don't see how that requires that something like dot_product,  sum or any other function which takes vector or matrix needs to be implemented in terms of the elementary operations.  Just like we have a custom dot_product vari now, we create a custom dot_product expression template in the new pattern.  The same would hold for other more complex functions (e.g., inverse quadratic forms).  Going further on that though, won't this make our compilation times *much* worse though?

Cheers,
Marcus

